# Extra harness-hash patterns for intent-eval-core (consumed by harness-hash.sh).
# Each non-comment line is a glob, relative to the repo root, of an
# engineer-owned policy artifact to hash-pin alongside the canonical defaults.

# 3kye.6 / DR-049 — the rubric-floor anti-realignment guard. Self-pinned so the
# floor cannot be weakened in the same PR that weakens the guard: any byte change
# to this file fails `audit-harness verify` until a separate, reviewable
# `audit-harness init` re-pins it.
scripts/check-rubric-floor.ts

# iec-lint-rollout (bd_000-projects-bbi6) — the non-JS lint policy surface.
# lint.yml enforces yamllint + actionlint + markdownlint; the vendored
# yamllint config is the YAML rule set it applies. Both are pinned so a
# silent edit (e.g. relaxing a rule to `disable` or weakening the workflow
# to `|| true`) fails `audit-harness verify` until a separate, reviewable
# `audit-harness init` re-pins it — the same self-pin rationale the sibling
# repos apply to their CI workflows + vendored policy files.
.github/workflows/lint.yml
.audit-harness/configs/.yamllint.yml
